ttention, crew atmosphere. Communication difficulty and egocentric may affect crew cooperation but he creates positive atmosphere. Egocentric may be a risk but not as severe as nasty remarks. Also not willing to further education may affect adaptability.\n\nCandidate B has strong stress handling, conscientiousness, weather assessment, but communication issues are severe (nasty remarks) and weak memory for numbers affects attention.\n\nThus I might lean towards Candidate C as best overall. However we need to discuss A and D later. But we can still give provisional recommendation for C, while noting need for more info on A and D. That aligns with covering all candidates later.\n\nThus I will state my current recommendation: Candidate C. I will reference Agent 2's support for C and Agent 3's earlier recommendation for B, and explain why I think C's strengths outweigh B's communication issues, but also note concerns about C's egocentric attitude and lack of willingness for further education, and that we still need to evaluate A and D.\n\nProvide evidence: quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, 100% reliability, positive crew atmosphere, excellent attention. Concerns: difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education.\n\nThus I will argue that despite communication issues, C's overall fit is stronger.\n\nProceed."}
