ers, but difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric, not willing to further education. Which is stronger? The panel seems leaning to C. As Agent 3, we can reconsider. We need to provide a focused argumentative contribution, referencing prior discussion, using explicit facts, and state our current recommendation. We can either maintain B or shift to C. Given the strong arguments from others, we might shift to C, but we need to justify why we change. We can argue that B's nasty remarks and weak memory for numbers are more severe than C's communication difficulty and egocentric attitude, especially for crew cooperation and attention. So we can change vote to C.\n\nThus public message: I acknowledge the points raised, note B's serious communication issues (nasty remarks) and weak memory for numbers, which affect crew cooperation and attention, while C's strengths in decision quality, calmness, reliability, attention, and concern for others outweigh his communication difficulty and egocentric attitude. Therefore I now recommend Candidate C.\n\nProvide METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nProceed."}
